{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_27948b586511e0b000f3b401845879caf57476ac550f506aeaf5464996ec2342", "title": "Cyril Havermans", "text": "Cyril Havermans is a Dutch musician, best known for being in the progressive rock band, Focus.", "score": 33.5555}, {"id": "hp_doc_12773a7beeef30d5c731cfe27b77bb93ecebea07e8c13013a7045c8d4fc8ac49", "title": "Cyril (album)", "text": "Cyril is the first solo album by Dutch singer-songwriter Cyril Havermans. It was recorded in 1973 after Havermans left Dutch progressive rock band Focus. The parting was amicable and came about partly as a result of Havermans' desire to include more vocal content (Focus are primarily an instrumental band). His erstwhile band-mates contribute much instrumentation to the album.", "score": 32.2779}, {"id": "hp_doc_aa2c6200d84bc4c562384517c423b3b77c62954c269947fad352a35972e34cda", "title": "Focus II", "text": "Focus II (better known as its international title Moving Waves) is the second studio album from the Dutch rock band Focus, released in October 1971 on Imperial Records. Following the departure of Martin Dresden and Hans Cleuver in 1970, the band recruited Cyril Havermans on bass and Pierre van der Linden on drums and proceeded to work on new material. The album includes \"Hocus Pocus\", the group's most successful single, and \"Eruption\", a 22-minute track based on the opera \"Euridice\" by Jacopo Peri.", "score": 22.2591}], "remaining_searches": 2}
